 61CU c  {+61}Cu produced and identified by 1937Th01 (deuteron bombardment of Ni
 61CU2c  by 5 MeV deuterons followed by chemical separation), and 1937Ri01      
 61CU3c  (E=9 MeV alpha bombardment of Ni, chemical separation).                
 61CU c  2010Vi07: measured spin, magnetic dipole moment and electric quadrupole
 61CU2c  moment, hyperfine structure study at ISOLDE-CERN using collinear and   
 61CU3c  in-source laser spectroscopy                                           
 61CU d  Theory:                                                                
 61CU d  1976Da02; calculated mass excess.                                      
 61CU d  1995Zh26: effective boson numbers                                      
 61CU d  1995Ba78: binding energy, isotope shift, ground state                  
 61CU d  1994Ku01: surface pairing                                              
 61CU d  2002Ca48: large-scale shell model calculations.                        
